From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: qcom: report an attached partner when gen1 starts toggling

Restarting the gen1 state machine with a partner still attached, e.g.
booting with a dock plugged in, leaves the CC state unchanged and raises
no type-c-change, so TCPM sat in TOGGLING forever.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port_gen1.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port_gen1.c
@@ -373,6 +373,8 @@
 	unsigned int role;
 	unsigned int try_src = 0;
 	unsigned int try_snk = 0;
+	unsigned int status4;
+	bool attached = false;
 	int ret;
 
 	switch (port_type) {
@@ -414,9 +416,20 @@
 		goto out;
 
 	ret = gen1_typec_set_power_role(port, role);
+	if (ret)
+		goto out;
+
+	/* a partner that stays attached raises no type-c-change */
+	if (!regmap_read(port->regmap, port->base + TYPEC_STATUS_4_REG,
+			 &status4))
+		attached = status4 & CC_ATTACHED;
 
 out:
 	mutex_unlock(&port->lock);
+
+	if (attached && port->tcpm_port)
+		tcpm_cc_change(port->tcpm_port);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
